@baseUrl = http://localhost:4010
@token = tok_acme_admin

### ban a customer with an audit reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_12/ban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Chargeback abuse" }

### repeating the ban is a safe no-op, not a duplicate event
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_12/ban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Chargeback abuse" }

### unban
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_12/unban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Appeal accepted" }

### repeating the unban is also a no-op
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_12/unban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Appeal accepted" }

### a reason is mandatory
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_12/ban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### support staff may ban
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_acme/customers/cus_acme_13/ban
Authorization: Bearer tok_acme_support
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Suspicious refund pattern" }

### an Acme token cannot ban a Globex customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_globex/customers/cus_globex_01/ban
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Cross-tenant attempt" }

### a platform admin can
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/ten_globex/customers/cus_globex_01/ban
Authorization: Bearer tok_platform
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Platform-level fraud review" }
